            <ArticleTitle>Continuous Structured Population Models for Daphnia magna.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2627-2648</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11538-017-0344-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We continue our efforts in modeling Daphnia magna, a species of water flea, by proposing a continuously structured population model incorporating density-dependent and density-independent fecundity and mortality rates. We collected new individual-level data to parameterize the individual demographics relating food availability and individual daphnid growth. Our model is fit to experimental data using the generalized least-squares framework, and we use cross-validation and Akaike Information Criteria to select hyper-parameters. We present our confidence intervals on parameter estimates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
